AI provider: send the workspace header an unscoped Anthropic key requires

An Anthropic API key that is not scoped to a workspace is refused unless
every request carries anthropic-workspace-id ("This API key is not scoped to
a workspace, so this request must include the anthropic-workspace-id
header"), which is what the Intelligent copilot hit. Every request to the AI
provider - chat, JSON analysis, the copilot, OCR, embeddings, translation,
speech, and transcription when it is the same provider - now carries
AI_WORKSPACE_ID as that header, plus any headers in AI_API_HEADERS (a JSON
object; it cannot override the key or the content type, and invalid JSON is
ignored rather than half-sent). Both are server environment only, like the
key. Tests: packages/ai headers.test.ts.

